{
  "core_question": "What analyses must the hospital board conduct across clinical, legal, and financial domains to evaluate a private‑equity acquisition involving conversion to for‑profit status, sale‑leaseback of real estate, and spin‑out of a charitable foundation?",
  "rationale": "The transaction touches patient care standards (healthcare), tax‑exempt status and regulatory approvals (legal), and valuation, financing structure, and cash‑flow projections (finance).",
  "routes": ["healthcare", "legal", "finance"],
  "sub_questions": {
    "healthcare": "What are the key clinical and operational impacts of converting a rural nonprofit community hospital to for‑profit status, including effects on patient care quality metrics, workforce retention, Medicare/Medicaid eligibility, and compliance with CMS regulations?",
    "legal": "What legal steps and regulatory approvals are required to (1) convert the hospital’s operating entity from nonprofit to for‑profit, (2) spin out a charitable foundation holding transaction proceeds while preserving tax‑exempt status, and (3) execute a sale‑leaseback of the real estate, including considerations under IRS 501(c)(3) rules, state licensing laws, fiduciary duties, and antitrust concerns?",
    "finance": "How should the board evaluate the financial feasibility of the private‑equity acquisition, specifically analyzing the valuation of the hospital assets, structuring of the sale‑leaseback financing (lease terms, interest rates, tax implications), projected cash flows, return on investment for the sponsor, and impact on the hospital’s debt capacity?"
  },
  "requires_recency_disclosure": true,
  "recency_notes": "IRS 501(c)(3) sale‑leaseback guidance, CMS regulations on nonprofit hospitals, recent state licensing changes, and current market rates for lease financing may have been updated after the specialists’ training cutoffs."
}
